From 2e50a069ece19d96fe8aedd2462904763d10c37f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: V-PACE <yocto@vpace>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 02:53:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] screen-share: mirror the output's full physical resolution

screen-share.so builds the buffer it hands to a mirrored output (e.g. the
RDP backend in weston-remote-display) from weston_output's logical
(post-scale) width/height, not its physical current_mode size. The
capture step earlier in the same file (shared_output_repainted()) already
reads the compositor's framebuffer at full current_mode resolution into
so->cache_image -- the extra detail exists in memory -- but
shared_output_get_shm_buffer() then allocates the outgoing shm buffer at
the smaller logical size, and shared_output_update()'s composite applies
a current_scale downsample on the way out. For a scale=1 output this is a
no-op; for a HiDPI-scaled output (scale=2 in weston-rdp.ini, paired with
a 2x synthetic EDID in weston-force-output) it silently throws away
exactly the resolution the scale was set up to capture.

This is a known, intentional simplification upstream, not a bug: the
function's own comment says the remote surface is 'scale=1... so if the
output has a different scale... this is effectively undone (possibly by
throwing away pixels in a later step).' We want that step to keep the
pixels instead, since the destination here is an RDP-mirrored head unit
viewed fullscreen on a much higher-resolution monitor, where the
downsample-then-upscale round trip is exactly the pixelation we're
trying to avoid.

Three changes, all in compositor/screen-share.c:
  - shared_output_get_shm_buffer(): allocate width/height from
    output->current_mode instead of output->width/height, so the shm
    buffer (and its stride, mmap size, and damage region, all derived
    from the same locals) is sized for the full physical resolution.
  - output_compute_transform(): drop the trailing current_scale
    pixman_transform_scale(). so->cache_image and the shm buffer are now
    both current_mode-sized, so the copy is 1:1; rotation/flip handling
    for a real rotated panel is untouched.
  - shared_output_update(): the final pixman_image_composite32() call
    copies output->current_mode->width/height instead of
    output->width/height, so the whole buffer is copied rather than just
    its top-left logical-sized corner.

The PIXMAN_FILTER_NEAREST/BILINEAR selection a few lines above is left
as-is -- it becomes a harmless no-op once the transform carries no scale.

Only takes effect where scale != 1 is actually configured. At the
default scale=1 this is a no-op (current_mode and the old logical
width/height are the same value), so it doesn't affect a normal
scale=1 output.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 compositor/screen-share.c | 19 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/compositor/screen-share.c b/compositor/screen-share.c
index 305bab1..6a8b708 100644
--- a/compositor/screen-share.c
+++ b/compositor/screen-share.c
@@ -440,8 +440,12 @@ shared_output_get_shm_buffer(struct shared_output *so)
 	int fd;
 	unsigned char *data;
 
-	width = so->output->width;
-	height = so->output->height;
+	/* Use the output's physical (current_mode) size rather than its
+	 * logical (post-scale) size, so a HiDPI-scaled output's mirror
+	 * buffer carries the full resolution instead of being silently
+	 * downsampled back to scale=1 in shared_output_update(). */
+	width = so->output->current_mode->width;
+	height = so->output->current_mode->height;
 	stride = width * 4;
 
 	/* If the size of the output changed, we free the old buffers and
@@ -571,9 +575,10 @@ output_compute_transform(struct weston_output *output,
 		break;
 	}
 
-	pixman_transform_scale(transform, NULL,
-			       pixman_fixed_1 * output->current_scale,
-			       pixman_fixed_1 * output->current_scale);
+	/* No post-scale here: so->cache_image and the shm buffer are now
+	 * both sized from current_mode (see shared_output_get_shm_buffer()),
+	 * so a 1:1 copy is correct. Scaling by current_scale on top of that
+	 * would sample cache_image out of its own bounds. */
 }
 
 static void
@@ -674,8 +679,8 @@ shared_output_update(struct shared_output *so)
 				 0, 0, /* src_x, src_y */
 				 0, 0, /* mask_x, mask_y */
 				 0, 0, /* dest_x, dest_y */
-				 so->output->width, /* width */
-				 so->output->height /* height */);
+				 so->output->current_mode->width, /* width */
+				 so->output->current_mode->height /* height */);
 
 	pixman_image_set_transform(sb->pm_image, NULL);
 	pixman_image_set_clip_region32(sb->pm_image, NULL);
-- 
